# Normalise line endings in the repository, not in the working copy.
#
# Windows checkouts get CRLF locally (which editors there expect), but every
# file is stored — and therefore shipped to CI and to Vercel — with LF. Without
# this, a Windows machine and a Linux runner disagree about every line of every
# file, and every diff shows the whole file as changed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# These two are line-ending sensitive: a CRLF in a shell script is a syntax
# error, and a CRLF in a YAML block scalar can change what the run step means.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Binary-ish files that must never be line-ending converted.
*.svg text eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
